    "result_text": "The suite has a single test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required rejecting a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a 400 response. The field lives on `Owner` and is handled in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\nI added a guard in `OwnerRestControllerV1`:\n\n- A new `rejectFutureRegistrationDate(LocalDate)` helper that throws `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(List.of(\"registrationDate\"))` when a non-null supplied date `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`. That exception is already mapped to **400 Bad Request** by `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.\n- It's invoked in `addOwner` right after `validateRequiredFields`, checking the raw supplied value **before** the business-day adjustment. A `null` (omitted) date is left alone so it still defaults to the server date, keeping existing behavior intact.\n\nThe acceptance test `errorRejectsFutureDate` (posts `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"`, expects 400) and the full suite both pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
